{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "13556592",
      "title": "Creating a Custom useInput Hook",
      "sourceHash": "17f326181e15345f66f6087986bb0e2169a775c2012c174a582f056004bbf456",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.33,
          "end": 2.94,
          "en": "Now with all those steps taken,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.94,
          "end": 6.09,
          "en": "the code in this StateLogin JSX file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.09,
          "end": 8.64,
          "en": "got a little bit leaner.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.64,
          "end": 10.59,
          "en": "But of course, if we're honest,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.59,
          "end": 13.44,
          "en": "most of the code that we had to write here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.44,
          "end": 18.44,
          "en": "is about managing the entered values and didEdit states",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.51,
          "end": 22.599,
          "en": "and about updating those states with the handleInputChange",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.599,
          "end": 25.41,
          "en": "and the handleInputBlur functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.41,
          "end": 28.23,
          "en": "And we therefore also might wanna outsource",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.23,
          "end": 30.36,
          "en": "and reuse this code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.36,
          "end": 32.73,
          "en": "And how could we do that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.73,
          "end": 35.34,
          "en": "Well, with help of a custom hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.34,
          "end": 39.27,
          "en": "And we need a custom hook because we are managing some state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.27,
          "end": 41.49,
          "en": "in that code that should be outsourced,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.49,
          "end": 44.613,
          "en": "and therefore we can't use a regular function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.87,
          "end": 49.8,
          "en": "But we can now build such a custom hook by, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.8,
          "end": 52.92,
          "en": "adding a hooks folder in that source folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.92,
          "end": 55.38,
          "en": "And as you learned, that name is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.38,
          "end": 57.54,
          "en": "doesn't have to be named hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.54,
          "end": 61.773,
          "en": "And in there, we could add a file named useInput.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.94,
          "end": 64.59,
          "en": "Doesn't need to be JSX",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.59,
          "end": 68.07300000000001,
          "en": "because I'm not going to write any JSX code in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.36,
          "end": 74.36,
          "en": "And here we can now export a useInput function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.97,
          "end": 77.25,
          "en": "and it must start with use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.25,
          "end": 80.7,
          "en": "as you learned in the custom hooks section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.7,
          "end": 84.63,
          "en": "so that it's identified as a hook function by React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.63,
          "end": 87.813,
          "en": "and the rules of hooks are applied to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.01,
          "end": 93.53999999999999,
          "en": "And then we can grab this state management code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 93.53999999999999,
          "end": 96.393,
          "en": "copy it, and add it to useInput,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 97.22999999999999,
          "end": 100.36,
          "en": "though we'll of course have to tweak it a little bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 101.31,
          "end": 104.22,
          "en": "because my idea here now is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 104.22,
          "end": 108.3,
          "en": "that I build a useInput hook that should be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108.3,
          "end": 112.22999999999999,
          "en": "once per input element we have in our form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 112.22999999999999,
          "end": 114.33,
          "en": "So if we have two input elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 114.33,
          "end": 116.493,
          "en": "we need to call the hook twice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 118.2,
          "end": 121.35,
          "en": "So instead of managing some object state here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 121.35,
          "end": 125.46,
          "en": "that groups the values of multiple inputs together,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 125.46,
          "end": 128.763,
          "en": "I just want to manage one single value here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 129.84,
          "end": 131.73,
          "en": "and therefore I'll rename that state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 131.73,
          "end": 133.863,
          "en": "from enteredValues to EnteredValue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 135.42,
          "end": 139.89,
          "en": "and my initial value should be settable from outside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 139.89,
          "end": 143.25,
          "en": "so that we could also pre-populate an input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 143.25,
          "end": 145.893,
          "en": "with any value of our choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 147.12,
          "end": 150.96,
          "en": "Therefore here we could accept a default value parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 150.96,
          "end": 152.61,
          "en": "in this custom hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 152.61,
          "end": 155.99,
          "en": "and use this to set the default state here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 155.99,
          "end": 157.773,
          "en": "of the entered value state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 158.94,
          "end": 162.813,
          "en": "And then here of course, we must import useState from React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 165.6,
          "end": 167.28300000000002,
          "en": "So that's one piece of state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 168.251,
          "end": 172.62,
          "en": "DidEdit now also should not manage some object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 172.62,
          "end": 175.68,
          "en": "that combines the states of multiple inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 175.68,
          "end": 179.07,
          "en": "but instead just manage a single value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 179.07,
          "end": 181.77,
          "en": "where I again will start with false,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 181.77,
          "end": 184.14,
          "en": "though we could of course also accept this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 184.14,
          "end": 187.803,
          "en": "as a parameter here if we would wanna make it configurable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 188.7,
          "end": 190.62,
          "en": "Now that we've got the state in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 190.62,
          "end": 193.62,
          "en": "we'll also have to bring the functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 193.62,
          "end": 196.653,
          "en": "that update that state into the custom hook though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 197.57999999999998,
          "end": 201.76,
          "en": "So I will copy handleInputChange and handleInputBlur",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 202.95,
          "end": 205.713,
          "en": "and add those to my custom hook here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 207.54,
          "end": 211.38,
          "en": "And since we're now just managing one single input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 211.38,
          "end": 213.42000000000002,
          "en": "and one single value in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 213.42000000000002,
          "end": 216.603,
          "en": "we can also simplify those functions here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 217.47,
          "end": 219,
          "en": "And, for example, again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 219,
          "end": 222.15,
          "en": "just expect to get the event object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 222.15,
          "end": 223.78,
          "en": "on handleInputChange",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 225.18,
          "end": 229.2,
          "en": "and then set the entered value, not values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 229.2,
          "end": 232.083,
          "en": "to event.target.value again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 234.06,
          "end": 238.23,
          "en": "and setDidEdit here simply to false",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 238.23,
          "end": 240.87,
          "en": "because, again, we just have a single inputs value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 240.87,
          "end": 242.17,
          "en": "which we're managing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 243.72,
          "end": 248.613,
          "en": "And then handleInputBlur, we therefore setDidEdit to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 250.26,
          "end": 254.043,
          "en": "So now we got much simpler code in this custom hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 255.78,
          "end": 257.82,
          "en": "Now of course, just having the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 257.82,
          "end": 262.38,
          "en": "and these functions in here won't do much for us though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 262.38,
          "end": 266.13,
          "en": "What we need to do is expose them to the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 266.13,
          "end": 268.62,
          "en": "where this hook should be used.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 268.62,
          "end": 272.67,
          "en": "And therefore, here I'll return a value in my custom hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 272.67,
          "end": 274.89,
          "en": "and you could return an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 274.89,
          "end": 276.93,
          "en": "to group multiple values together,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 276.93,
          "end": 279.963,
          "en": "or what I'll do, return an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 281.07,
          "end": 285.213,
          "en": "And here I will then return my value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 286.2,
          "end": 290.163,
          "en": "so this enteredValue state which we're managing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 291.09000000000003,
          "end": 292.26,
          "en": "I'll expose it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 292.26,
          "end": 295.683,
          "en": "through a value property in this returned object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 297,
          "end": 300.37,
          "en": "And I'll also add pointers at handleInputChange",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 302.036,
          "end": 305.423,
          "en": "and handleInputBlur to this returned object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 306.63,
          "end": 310.05,
          "en": "so that this object also has these properties,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 310.05,
          "end": 313.983,
          "en": "which contain values that point at these functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 315.24,
          "end": 318.63,
          "en": "Now with that, didEdit is not getting used yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 318.63,
          "end": 320.403,
          "en": "but that will change soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 321.3,
          "end": 324.39,
          "en": "What I wanna change right away is this identifier here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 324.39,
          "end": 328.413,
          "en": "which should no longer be accepted on handleInputBlur.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 329.85,
          "end": 332.82,
          "en": "But with that, we now got a first basic draft",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 332.82,
          "end": 337.17,
          "en": "of this use input hook, and we can start using this hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 337.17,
          "end": 340.53,
          "en": "And for that, I'll go back to the StateLogin JSX file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 340.53,
          "end": 344.65,
          "en": "and in there, we can now get rid of this state here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 346.467,
          "end": 350.22,
          "en": "and get rid of handleInputChange and handleInputBlur,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 350.22,
          "end": 353.823,
          "en": "and also of these commented-out functions here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 354.9,
          "end": 357.453,
          "en": "so that we got much leaner code in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 358.32,
          "end": 360.52,
          "en": "and instead call useInput",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 362.28,
          "end": 364.98,
          "en": "and, of course, import useInput",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 364.98,
          "end": 368.373,
          "en": "from the useInput.js file in the hooks folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 370.02,
          "end": 373.41,
          "en": "We can now also get rid of the useState import here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 373.41,
          "end": 375.99,
          "en": "because I'm not managing any custom state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 375.99,
          "end": 377.58299999999997,
          "en": "in this component anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 379.83,
          "end": 382.304,
          "en": "Instead, we have useInput,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 382.304,
          "end": 385.77,
          "en": "and useInput wants the default value of the input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 385.77,
          "end": 388.68,
          "en": "to which it should belong as an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 388.68,
          "end": 390.93,
          "en": "So therefore, here I'll pass an empty string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 391.86,
          "end": 394.743,
          "en": "and we'll get back an object which we can destructure,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 395.58,
          "end": 397.62,
          "en": "and that object will have a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 397.62,
          "end": 399.99,
          "en": "to which I'll assign an alias here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 399.99,
          "end": 403.02,
          "en": "which I'll name emailValue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 403.02,
          "end": 407.15999999999997,
          "en": "because I plan on using useInput multiple times",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 407.15999999999997,
          "end": 408.81,
          "en": "for different inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 408.81,
          "end": 410.67,
          "en": "Therefore, I need an alias here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 410.67,
          "end": 413.703,
          "en": "to clearly identify which value this is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 415.53,
          "end": 419.28,
          "en": "I will also get handleInputChange out of here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 419.28,
          "end": 422.823,
          "en": "and alias it to handleEmailChange,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 424.95,
          "end": 426.67,
          "en": "and get handleInputBlur",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 427.92,
          "end": 430.9,
          "en": "and assign an alias of handleEmailBlur",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 434.88,
          "end": 437.523,
          "en": "so that I'm using my custom hook like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 439.44,
          "end": 442.98,
          "en": "Now with that, that validation logic here won't work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 442.98,
          "end": 447.87,
          "en": "but we can now use the emailValue to assign it as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 447.87,
          "end": 450.723,
          "en": "for the value prop on the email input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 452.67,
          "end": 457.59000000000003,
          "en": "And here for onBlur, we no longer need this wrapper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 457.59000000000003,
          "end": 460.65,
          "en": "because we no longer need this identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 460.65,
          "end": 464.49,
          "en": "because we now have a dedicated handleEmailChange function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 464.49,
          "end": 467.01,
          "en": "since this hook is about managing the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 467.01,
          "end": 468.33299999999997,
          "en": "of a single input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 469.17,
          "end": 472.62,
          "en": "So therefore, this code down here can be simplified",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 472.62,
          "end": 474.49,
          "en": "to point at handleEmailBlur",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 476.1,
          "end": 478.533,
